<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<% content_for :description, "Who I am, how I work and what I am looking for. Ruby on Rails developer, remote first, comfortable across the stack from Hotwire to Sidekiq." %>

<section class="w-full">
  <h1 class="sr-only">About</h1>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8 pt-16">
    <%= render layout: "shared/panel" do %>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-6 text-white flex items-center gap-3">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-rocket text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        Who I am
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>I'm Victor. I write Ruby on Rails, front and back.</p>
        <p>It started the way it does for a lot of people my age: pulling apart websites to see what made them work. Epitech in Nantes came after, then a year in Seoul. I did C and C++ first, then a stretch of front-end in Angular and React. Rails arrived in 2024 and I stopped looking around.</p>
        <p>The things I've built tend to have real users behind them. A dashboard city agents use to run waste collection. An internal analytics tool. A nutrition app that's mine, that I keep running.</p>
        <p>French is my first language. I work in English, and I studied Chinese at university.</p>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%= render layout: "shared/panel" do %>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-6 text-white flex items-center gap-3">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        How I work
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>Eight months fully remote at Publidata shaped the way I work now. They handed me a scope and left me to organize it, and it turned out to suit me better than I expected.</p>
        <p>It's also where I got serious about AI. I've built a setup around it that covers planning and review as much as writing code, and I tear it up every few months because the tools keep moving. It's part of how I work now, not a gadget I bring out for show.</p>
        <p>I like small teams and agile that stays light. I want to be in on a feature while it's still an idea, not handed a ticket with every decision already made. And I try to leave code the next person can read without coming to ask me about it.</p>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%= render layout: "shared/panel" do %>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-6 text-white flex items-center gap-3">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-bullseye text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        What I'm looking for
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>I'm looking for a Rails job. Full stack, and I mean that literally: I'm as at home on the front as on the back.</p>
        <p>Remote, ideally. I've done it and it suits me, so it's the last thing I'd give up. Where the company sits matters less: France, elsewhere in Europe, further out. I'd move for the right one.</p>
        <p>Past that I don't have a long list. Something people actually use, a team small enough that I know what everyone is doing, a codebase old enough to have some history in it.</p>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%= render layout: "shared/panel" do %>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-6 text-white flex items-center gap-3">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-code text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        Technologies
      </h2>

      <% @skill_groups.each_with_index do |group, index| %>
        <div class="<%= "mb-8" unless index == @skill_groups.size - 1 %>">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-4 text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <i class="<%= group[:icon] %> text-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <%= group[:name] %>
          </h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 lg:grid-cols-6 gap-4">
            <% group[:technologies].each do |technology| %>
              <div class="flex flex-col items-center p-3 rounded-lg bg-white/5 hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors duration-200">
                <i class="<%= technology[:icon] %> text-3xl <%= technology[:color] %> mb-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="text-sm text-neutral-300"><%= technology[:name] %></span>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
